{
  "id": "Compound::DB00810 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Biperiden is likely to interact with Chrm1 through a series of molecular and cellular mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Biperiden binds to Chrm2, which is a key component of the muscarinic acetylcholine receptor family. This binding leads to the participation of Chrm2 in the broader acetylcholine receptor activity, ultimately resulting in the participation of Chrm1 in this process. The shared involvement of Chrm2 in multiple pathways, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity and muscarinic acetylcholine receptor activity, indicates a potential functional link between Biperiden and Chrm1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Biperiden influences Chrm1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
